        ]
      },
      "stats": {
        "additions": 65,
        "deletions": 5
      },
      "facts": [
        "Agent id the freebuff WEB CHAT uses for its gemini-thinker child (see agents/thinker/thinker-gemini.ts, spawned from agents/base-chat.ts). Distinct from the CLI's FREEBUFF_GEMINI_THINKER_AGENT_ID.",
        "The ONLY agents permitted to call the premium Gemini Pro model. Gemini Pro is not a user-pickable model, its only legitimate callers are these two thinker subagents (CLI + chat). The chat-completions endpoint rejects any other agent that requests Gemini Pro on an unbilled path.",
        "Whether the requested model is Gemini Pro, tolerating the dated snapshot suffix. Use this instead of `=== FREEBUFF_GEMINI_PRO_MODEL_ID` so a caller can't dodge a Gemini gate by sending the dated id.",
        "Suffix-tolerant: a dated variant of a premium id (e.g. a dated Kimi) must still count as premium so it can't dodge the premium daily rate cap."
      ],
      "title": "Shared/Core update: free-agents",
      "summary": "Shared/Core changes across 3 file(s) (+65/−5).",
      "tags": [],
      "prevSha": "ada3ef96ca89db5f972b36215e34e7663bafb539",
      "skip": false,
      "category": "Core",
      "significance": "minor",
      "day": "2026-06-22",
      "month": "2026-06",
      "hasDiff": true,
      "ai": {
        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Gate premium Gemini Pro to thinker subagents with suffix-tolerant",
        "summary": "Added `isFreebuffGeminiProAgent` gate in `common/src/constants/free-agents.ts` restricting premium Gemini Pro calls to CLI (`thinker-with-files-gemini`) and Web Chat (`thinker-gemini`) subagents. Introduced `freebuffModelIdMatches` in `common/src/constants/freebuff-models.ts` to tolerate dated snapshot suffixes (e.g., `-20260219`), preventing callers from bypassing gates by sending dated model IDs. This logic now applies to `isFreebuffGeminiProModelId` and `isFreebuffPremiumModelId` to enforce daily rate caps on dated variants. Scope covers shared core constants used by CLI and Web surfaces.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T16:11:03.587Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "If you use the free assistant on the website or in the terminal, you can no longer accidentally ask it to run the paid Gemini Pro model behind the scenes. The only pieces of the assistant that are allowed to talk to that expensive model are the two small 'thinker' helpers, one on the web and one in the terminal. The system now also recognizes dated versions of the model name (like 'gemini-3.1-pro-preview-20260219') as the same premium model, so someone can't trick it into using the paid one by appending a date. If you looked, you'd see the assistant quietly blocking any other part of itself from spending your free quota on Gemini Pro.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "01c6e9003d38",
        "at": "2026-09-17T20:23:47.268Z"
      },
